Package: qdp
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Ian Armour <ianmarmour@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: @DEPENDS@
Recommends: libva2, libva-drm2
Section: net
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/ianmarmour/qdp
Description: Quick Desktop Protocol: stream desktops over the network
 QDP streams a computer's desktop to other devices, and shows other
 computers' desktops, over QUIC with AV1 video. The qdp command is both the
 host, qdp serve, and a client, qdp connect.
 .
 The package lets the user at the machine create the virtual input devices
 the host plays a client's keyboard, mouse, touch, pens and passed-through
 devices through, and loads the kernel modules for them at boot. Its qdp
 service, off until turned on with systemctl enable --now qdp, serves from
 boot what the graphics card shows, the login screen included, so that
 devices can log in.
